	// zappy's bed for explaining, the curious mood. 22 bars, 49.79 s,
	// 104 a minute with three small steps up and one back. d with a
	// raised fourth (g#), the scale of wondering.
	//
	// the plan. three things, all from the ident. the motif: a4 d5 e5 a5
	// | f#5. the call: its first three notes alone (a d e), a question.
	// the floor: the ident's low b flat. and one new thing, a bounce: the
	// bass in quiet eighths, root, fifth, octave, fifth, ninth, fifth,
	// octave, fifth, which is the motif's own notes (d a e) kept turning.
	//
	// harmony, a bar each:
	//   1-4   d d d d            the bounce alone, then the motif (3-4)
	//   5-6   e/d e/d            the motif a step up: b e f# b | g#,
	//                            the raised fourth on top (wondering)
	//   7-8   d d                the motif, and its tail walks home f# e d
	//   9-12  g a g a            working it out: the call on g (d g a),
	//                            on a (e a b), again later in the bar,
	//                            then climbing e a b c#
	//   13    e/d                the climb's top, d6, held. louder.
	//   14    nothing            the gap: the call alone and quiet, a d e,
	//                            with no answer. every other voice rests.
	//   15-16 b flat             the turn, where the fact lands: the
	//                            ident's floor and a deep drum, and over
	//                            it the answer the call was owed, a5 f#5,
	//                            at half speed. the bounce has stopped.
	//   17-18 c                  the floor steps up; the motif on c
	//                            (g c d g | e), the way back opening.
	//   19-21 d d e/d            anyway: the bounce and the motif again
	//   22    d                  one short chord, the tune hops a d6 up to
	//                            home, and it stops.
	//
	// time: a tick off every beat, strict, like a mechanism. while it is
	// working things out the tempo steps up, 108 at bar 9, 112 at bar 11,
	// 116 at bar 13: thought speeding up. at the turn (bar 15) it is back
	// at 104 at once, and stays.
	//
	// loud and quiet: the bounce and the chords are p, the tune mp, bar 13
	// mf, the gap p, the turn's bass f (the loudest thing in the piece),
	// then back to p and mp. it is a bed: nothing is above mf but that
	// one low note.
